+# tidyjson
+
+tidyjson reformats a JSON file and writes the result back to the same file.
+
+## Install
+
+From a clone of this repository:
+
+```sh
+npm install -g .
+```
+
+This puts the `tidyjson` command on your `PATH`. It runs on Node.js.
+
+## Usage
+
+```sh
+tidyjson <file> [--indent N] [--sort-keys]
+```
+
+tidyjson overwrites `<file>` in place. Commit or copy the file first if you want to compare before and after.
+
+| Option | Effect |
+| --- | --- |
+| `--indent N` | Indent nested values by `N` spaces. |
+| `--sort-keys` | Sort object keys. |
+
+### Examples
+
+Reformat with 2-space indentation:
+
+```sh
+tidyjson config.json --indent 2
+```
+
+Reformat and sort keys, so that two files with the same data produce the same text:
+
+```sh
+tidyjson settings.json --indent 2 --sort-keys
+```
+
+## Invalid JSON
+
+If `<file>` does not parse as JSON, tidyjson exits with code 2 and leaves the file unchanged. Scripts can check for this:
+
+```sh
+tidyjson data.json --indent 2
+if [ $? -eq 2 ]; then
+  echo "data.json is not valid JSON" >&2
+fi
+```
+
+## Development
+
+Run the tests with:
+
+```sh
+npm test
+```
+
+This runs `node --test`.
